---
/** The privacy policy of the Errant Ant app, which the app's Settings → About → Privacy policy opens. */
---
<article class="policy">
  <h1>Errant Ant Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="policy-date">Effective date: 26 October 2026</p>

  <h2>Personal data we collect</h2>
  <p>
    We do not collect personal data. Errant Ant does not require an account, and it contains no analytics, advertising,
    tracking or crash reporting.
  </p>

  <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
  <p>
    Your books, reading progress, vocabulary, notes and boards are stored on your device and are not sent to us or to
    any third party. Dictionary lookups and translations run on your device.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>Errant Ant connects to the internet only when you use a feature that needs it:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Project Gutenberg, when you browse its catalog or download a book.</li>
    <li>GitHub, when you download a dictionary or a translation pack.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These services receive the information sent with any internet request, such as your IP address, and handle it under
    their own privacy policies: <a href="https://www.gutenberg.org/policy/privacy_policy.html">Project Gutenberg</a> and
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete your library and learning data at any time in Settings → About → Reset all data. To remove
    everything, including downloaded dictionaries and translation packs, uninstall Errant Ant and delete its data folder.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this Privacy Policy. Changes are posted on this page with a new effective date.</p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>Questions about this Privacy Policy: <a href="mailto:dev@buggylaggy.com">dev@buggylaggy.com</a></p>
</article>
